@startuml
title SysMon - Spawn LLM Server Sequence Diagram

participant "SysMon Frontend" as Frontend
participant "SysMon Backend" as Backend
participant "SysMon Authentication System" as Auth
participant "Ollama Runtime" as Ollama

note over Frontend
  Admin (Tier 1, 2 or 3) opens the LLM console,
  pastes a HuggingFace model repository, sets context
  length, CPU/GPU split and server port, then clicks Spawn.
end note

== Spawn ==
Frontend -> Backend : POST /v1/llms\nAuthorization: Bearer token\nIdempotency-Key: key\n{modelRepo, contextLength,\ncpuGpuSplit, port, computeGroupId}
Backend -> Auth : GET /v1/auth/validate\nAuthorization: Bearer token
Auth --> Backend : 200 OK {userId, tier}\nor 401 Unauthorized

alt Token missing, invalid or expired
  Backend --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\n{code, message}
else Caller may not spawn LLMs or use the chosen Compute Group
  Backend --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden\n{code, message}
else Compute Group does not exist
  Backend --> Frontend : 404 Not Found\n{code, message}
else Data invalid (empty modelRepo, bad port, missing fields)
  Backend --> Frontend : 422 Unprocessable Entity\n{code, field, message}
else All checks passed
  Backend -> Backend : Ensure Ollama runtime is available

  alt Ollama missing on host
    Backend -> Ollama : installOllama()
    alt Install failed
      Ollama --> Backend : error
      Backend --> Frontend : 503 Service Unavailable\n{code, message}
    else Install succeeded
      Ollama --> Backend : installed
    end
  else Ollama already available
    note right of Backend : Skip install
  end

  Backend -> Backend : Estimate model resource requirements
  Backend -> Backend : Validate against Compute Group limits

  alt Model exceeds Compute Group (CPU / RAM / GPU)
    Backend --> Frontend : 409 Conflict\n{code, message, details: resource}
  else Chosen port already in use
    Backend --> Frontend : 409 Conflict\n{code, field: port, message}
  else Validation passed
    Backend -> Ollama : POST /api/pull\n{model: modelRepo}
    Ollama --> Backend : 200 OK (model cached)\nor error

    alt Model pull failed
      Backend --> Frontend : 502 Bad Gateway\n{code, message}
    else Model ready
      Backend -> Ollama : Start server on port\nwith model and parameters
      alt Server start failed
        Ollama --> Backend : error
        Backend -> Backend : Mark instance Failed
        Backend --> Frontend : 502 Bad Gateway\n{code, message}
      else Server started
        Ollama --> Backend : listening
        Backend -> Backend : Register running LLM instance
        Backend --> Frontend : 201 Created\nLocation: /v1/llms/{llmId}\n{llmId, modelRepo, port, status,\ncomputeGroupId, endpoint, createdAt}
      end
    end
  end
end

note over Frontend
  After an error the Frontend shows the reason.
  The admin may correct the form (port, model,
  Compute Group) and send the request again.
end note

@enduml
